%% title: `Daemon Runtime Lifecycle State Machine`
%% summary: Legal daemon runtime ownership transitions after bootstrap reaches a live daemon.
%% commentary: This machine models `RuntimeComposition::start()`, `RuntimeLifecycle`, and the fail-closed startup path in daemon composition. Every edge is a real event or guard in code, and every failure terminal is observable through a typed caller error from the active command.
%% notes: explicit RuntimeLifecycle states only | startup failure rolls back to stopped | no direct Running to Stopped success path
%% recovery_rules: If startup fails before Running, the active caller gets a typed runtime/startup error and doctor does not return a report. | If the daemon reaches Running, later command-specific or doctor-specific state machines own the next visible outcome.
%% terminal_classes: StartupFailed is a caller-facing startup dependency error with rollback to Stopped. | Running is the success state that permits request serving. | StoppedAfterShutdown is the normal shutdown terminal.
%% sets: daemon
flowchart TD
    A["<b>Stopped</b>"] -->|start_requested| D["PreparingRuntime"]
    D -->|prepare_runtime err| X["StartupFailed
caller: typed runtime error
doctor: no report"]
    D -->|prepare_runtime ok| E["ActivatingRuntime"]
    E -->|activate_runtime ok| F["Running"]
    E -->|activate_runtime err| X
    F -->|begin_shutdown| G["Draining"]
    G -->|stop| H["StoppedAfterShutdown"]

    classDef happy fill:#14532d,color:#ffffff,stroke:#14532d,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef error fill:#7f1d1d,color:#ffffff,stroke:#7f1d1d,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef neutral fill:#e2e8f0,color:#111827,stroke:#334155,stroke-width:2px;

    class A,F,H happy;
    class X error;
    class D,E,G neutral;
